# VL10k, sections a + b: section b is cut off and coupled back while the
# train stands. The DLLs keep their state through it, as in RTS (a DLL is
# bound to its car once, 0x5026FC; 0x4F995C makes the groups again):
# section a keeps its reverser, section b comes back as a's slave.
#
#   openrts-train-check <RTS root> --dll tsrLoco_VL10k-1461 vl10k-1461a vl10k-1461b --script tests/data/vl10k_couple.script
0    expect panto == 3          # Init with a running start raised the pantographs
1    switch 38 1                # K_STR key to neutral and forward: Switched sets Engine::Reverse
2    switch 38 2
3    expect reverse == 1
3    expect_car 1 bound == 1    # section b: its DLL bound and initialised
3    expect_car 1 master == 0   # as a's slave
4    cut 1                      # b uncoupled (cocks closed)
4.5  expect reverse == 1        # a kept its state: no second Init
4.5  expect alive == 1
6    couple                     # b back on, its control cable connected
6.5  expect reverse == 1
6.5  expect key38 == 2
6.5  expect_car 1 bound == 1    # the same b, still bound
6.5  expect_car 1 master == 0   # a's slave again
8    switch B_S 1               # "S": the first notch
9    switch B_S 0
12   expect throttle >= 1
12   expect_car 1 throttle >= 1 # the slave follows the master's controller again
# ...but does not pull: VL10k's LostMaster cleared the master's commands to
# it (var[4]: breaker, fans, positions), and RTS does not Init a coupled car
# again, so b waits for the driver to give them again. Without the cut it
# pulls 29 kN here; a second Init (running) would have made it pull too.
12   expect_car 1 force == 0
12   expect alive == 1
